|url-status=live
}}</ref> In the same month macroeconomist [[James K. Galbraith]] used the 25th Annual Milton Friedman Distinguished Lecture to launch a sweeping attack against the consensus for monetarist economics and argued that Keynesian economics were far more relevant for tackling the emerging crises.<ref>{{cite conference
|url=http://utip.gov.utexas.edu/papers/CollapseofMonetarismdelivered.pdf
|title=The Collapse of Monetarism and the Irrelevance of the New Monetary Consensus
